 "intro_zh": "库克早期农业遗址（英語：Kuk Early Agricultural Site）是大洋洲国家巴布亞紐幾內亞的一座考古遺址，位於该国本岛新几内亚岛中部高原的瓦吉河谷，海拔約1550公尺，在西高地省首府芒特哈根東北方約12-13公里处。這處沼澤形成於一個前湖盆地，由沖積扇或河流沉積物堆积而成。考古學家在此發現了早期農業排水系統的證據，該系統始於約9,000年前。它包括三種主要類型的排水溝，這些排水溝被用來將該地區改造成人工草地。當地原住民曾在遗址内种植芋頭、香蕉和甘蔗等作物。该遗址於2008年获聯合國教科文組織列為世界文化遺產，为巴布亚新几内亚第一处世界遗产。",
 "intro_zh_source": "wikipedia",
 "intro_en": "Kuk Early Agricultural Site consists of 116 ha of swamps in the western highlands of New Guinea 1,500 metres above sea-level. Archaeological excavation has revealed the landscape to be one of wetland reclamation worked almost continuously for 7,000, and possibly for 10,000 years. It contains well-preserved archaeological remains demonstrating the technological leap which transformed plant exploitation to agriculture around 6,500 years ago. It is an excellent example of transformation of agricultural practices over time, from cultivation mounds to draining the wetlands through the digging of ditches with wooden tools. Kuk is one of the few places in the world where archaeological evidence suggests independent agricultural development and changes in agricultural practice over such a long period of time.",
 "intro_en_source": "unesco_official",
 "intro_local": "",
 "intro_local_source": null,
